/**
 * @defgroup PamsL3 pams/l3 — Level-3 Trigger Track Support
 * @ingroup Pams
 *
 * @brief TPC coordinate transformer and DAQ/L3 data-format headers supporting
 *        the STAR Level-3 online trigger track finder.
 *
 * `pams/l3/` contains the building blocks used by the L3 online trigger to
 * perform real-time TPC track reconstruction.  The core component is the
 * coordinate transformer class St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer, which converts
 * between raw detector-electronics coordinates, sector-local Cartesian
 * coordinates, and the global STAR coordinate system.
 *
 * The header files in `inc/` define the DAQ raw-data bank structures
 * (daqFormats.h), the L3 trigger output track and cluster formats
 * (L3Formats.h), TPC sector geometry constants (sector.h), and the coordinate
 * helper classes (St_l3_Coordinates.h).
 *
 * The offline equivalent of this code is in StRoot/StL3Maker.
 *
 * ## Coordinate systems
 *
 * Three coordinate systems are used:
 *
 * - **Raw** (`St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate`): pad, timebucket, row, sector —
 *   the native detector-electronics representation.
 * - **Local** (`St_l3_xyz_Coordinate` in sector frame): right-handed Cartesian
 *   system aligned with a single TPC sector; y points radially outward,
 *   x along pads, z along the drift direction.
 * - **Global** (`St_l3_xyz_Coordinate` in STAR frame): standard STAR
 *   coordinate system; sectors are rotated in 30° steps, with an x-mirror and
 *   z-flip for the east end-cap (sectors 13–24).
 *
 * @see St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer
 * @see St_l3_xyz_Coordinate
 * @see St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate
 */

/**
 * @class St_l3_xyz_Coordinate
 * @ingroup PamsL3
 * @brief Cartesian coordinate point (x, y, z) in either local or global frame.
 *
 * Stores three `double` components and provides inline setters and getters.
 * Used as both local-sector and global-STAR coordinate containers by
 * St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_xyz_Coordinate::St_l3_xyz_Coordinate()
 *   Default constructor: initialises all three components to 0.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_xyz_Coordinate::St_l3_xyz_Coordinate(double X, double Y, double Z)
 *   Constructs a coordinate point at (X, Y, Z).
 */

/**
 * @class St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate
 * @ingroup PamsL3
 * @brief Raw detector-electronics coordinate: (pad, timebucket, row, sector).
 *
 * All four components are stored as `double` to support sub-bin positions.
 * Sector numbers run 1–24; row numbers run 1–45 (13 inner + 32 outer rows).
 *
 * @fn St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate::St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate()
 *   Default constructor: initialises all four components to 0.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate::St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate(double P, double T, double R, double S)
 *   Constructs a coordinate point at (pad=P, timebucket=T, row=R, sector=S).
 */

/**
 * @class St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer
 * @ingroup PamsL3
 * @brief Transforms TPC hit coordinates between raw, local, and global frames.
 *
 * This class encapsulates the full TPC geometry (pad counts per row, radial
 * distances, sector rotation angles) as static tables and provides conversion
 * methods in both the raw→global and global→raw directions.
 *
 * ### Geometry tables (static)
 * - `numberOfPadsAtRow[45]`: number of pads in each of the 45 pad rows.
 * - `radialDistanceAtRow[45]`: radial distance of the pad-row centre from the
 *   beam axis (cm).  Inner rows are spaced 4.80 cm (rows 1–7) and 5.20 cm
 *   (rows 8–13); outer rows are spaced 2.00 cm (rows 14–45).
 * - `SectorSin[24]`, `SectorCos[24]`: sine and cosine of the sector rotation
 *   angles in 30° steps.
 * - `innerSectorPadPitch`: 0.335 cm (rows 1–13).
 * - `outerSectorPadPitch`: 0.67 cm (rows 14–45).
 *
 * ### Drift parameters
 * Three methods are available to initialise the z↔timebucket conversion:
 * - `Set_parameters_by_hand()`: uses hard-coded values (0.584 cm/tb, 201 cm
 *   drift length for both inner and outer sectors).
 * - `Get_parameters_from_db()`: reads drift velocity and geometry from the
 *   STAR TPC conditions database (offline only; requires `L3OFFLINE` build).
 * - `Use_transformation_provided_by_db()`: derives parameters by calling the
 *   official StTpcCoordinateTransform for representative inner/outer rows.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer()
 *   Default constructor.  Calls `Set_parameters_by_hand()` to initialise
 *   drift parameters with hard-coded values.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::raw_to_global(const St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate&, St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&)
 *   Converts a raw (pad, timebucket, row, sector) coordinate to the global
 *   STAR frame via an intermediate local-sector conversion.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::raw_to_local(const St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate&, St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&)
 *   Converts a raw coordinate to the local sector frame.
 *   Uses `innerSectorPadPitch` for rows ≤ 13 and `outerSectorPadPitch`
 *   otherwise; converts timebucket to z using the appropriate drift length.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::local_to_global(const St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate&, const St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&, St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&)
 *   Rotates a local-sector coordinate into the global frame using the
 *   pre-computed SectorSin/SectorCos tables.  Applies an x-mirror and z-flip
 *   for east end-cap sectors (sector > 12).
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::global_to_raw(const St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&, St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate&)
 *   Converts a global coordinate to raw by determining the sector, rotating
 *   back to local frame, then computing pad and timebucket.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::global_to_raw(int sector, int row, const St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&, St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate&)
 *   Overload that uses a known sector and row to bypass the sector-search step.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::global_to_local(const St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&, St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&, St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate&)
 *   Determines the sector by rotating the global x–y point in 30° steps
 *   until it falls within the first-sector wedge, then sets the local
 *   coordinate and the sector field of the raw coordinate.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::global_to_local(int sector, int row, const St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&, St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&)
 *   Overload that directly applies the inverse rotation matrix for a known
 *   sector and row without the iterative sector search.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::local_to_raw(const St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&, const St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&, St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate&)
 *   Converts a local coordinate to raw by searching for the matching pad row
 *   (nearest radial distance within 0.5 cm), then computing pad number and
 *   timebucket.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::local_to_raw(int row, const St_l3_xyz_Coordinate&, St_l3_ptrs_Coordinate&)
 *   Overload that uses a known pad-row number, avoiding the row search.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::Set_parameters_by_hand()
 *   Sets drift parameters to hard-coded values:
 *   `lengthPerTb` = 0.584 cm, `drift_length_inner` = `drift_length_outer` = 201 cm.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::Set_parameters_by_hand(double, double, double)
 *   Sets drift parameters explicitly: cm per timebucket, inner drift length
 *   (cm), outer drift length (cm).
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::Get_parameters_from_db()
 *   Reads drift velocity, gating-grid position, T0 corrections, and
 *   electronics parameters from the STAR TPC conditions database to compute
 *   `lengthPerTb`, `drift_length_inner`, and `drift_length_outer`.
 *   Only functional in offline builds with `L3OFFLINE` defined.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::Use_transformation_provided_by_db()
 *   Derives transformation parameters by calling the official
 *   `StTpcCoordinateTransform` for representative inner (row 5) and outer
 *   (row 30) pad rows at timebuckets 0 and 100.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::Print_parameters()
 *   Prints the current drift parameters to stdout.
 *
 * @fn St_l3_Coordinate_Transformer::Get_transformation_errors()
 *   Returns the count of out-of-range timebucket values encountered during
 *   coordinate conversion.
 */
